WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:18.169 --> 00:00:20.059
Well, we talked about, a little bit about,

00:00:20.059 --> 00:00:21.960
so there's arguments

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:24.480
saying that some people actually employ

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:25.829
violence as means

00:00:25.829 --> 00:00:28.400
to draw attention to draw international pressure

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:30.060
to help solve the issue,

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:31.570
so the argument goes

00:00:32.769 --> 00:00:34.610
the IRA

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:37.620
not employing violence in Ireland.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:39.800
We actually, well,

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:43.830
maybe in the UK people will petition to act but in United States or other parts of the world

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:46.460
nobody will care,

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:48.010
and their grievance will never be heard,

00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:50.520
and the problem will never be solved.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:54.540
So how would you respond to that argument?

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:59.160
I think it's a really good question, and it's

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:00.680
a very, very hard one

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:01.249
to answer honestly.

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:07.510
Because this is one of the most, this is a very
dangerous

00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:11.540
answer if you answer yes.

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:15.430
I think,

00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:19.250
I think however they're,

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:21.670
well I'll make two points. I think first of all

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:24.100
there are ways actually,

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:26.630
and the civil rights movement here

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:28.870
in a way was an example, well okay

00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:29.840
there were elements of violence

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:33.430
surrounding it, but it was basically

00:01:33.430 --> 00:01:35.030
a peaceful movement.

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:36.320
Ghandi: a peaceful movement.

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:37.860
You don't need to be violent,

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:40.140
but you do need to draw attention.

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:42.860
But violence is only way of drawing attention.

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:48.100
I think secondly, this is the debate I really
had with the IRA,

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:52.400
and shouldn't feign in the last two years before I
left office

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.400
my argument to them was,

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:58.680
and this is again the importance of the dialogue
we had, it's worth saying this.

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:00.460
When I first met

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:02.850
Gerry Adams and Martin McGuinness,

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:06.190
and it was obviously

00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:07.150
a huge thing

00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:09.869
for me to

00:02:09.869 --> 00:02:11.969
meet them and so on, and I remember there was a major

00:02:11.969 --> 00:02:13.739
questions as to whether I

00:02:13.739 --> 00:02:17.159
would shake hands with them or not.

00:02:17.159 --> 00:02:21.479
And I met them and I did shake hands with them.

00:02:21.479 --> 00:02:25.429
And later that day I went to visit a unionist area,

00:02:25.429 --> 00:02:27.049
and

00:02:27.049 --> 00:02:31.889
the whole of what looks very respectable kind of grannies

00:02:31.889 --> 00:02:36.599
sort of hanging around doing shopping and everything, and I went to this shopping percent, and they suddenly

00:02:36.599 --> 00:02:38.940
morphed into these screaming, shouting, bullying

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:43.619
grannies,

00:02:43.619 --> 00:02:46.899
waving rubber gloves at me, and I'm sorry,

00:02:46.899 --> 00:02:49.389
I got very alarmed. I was so so tired,

00:02:49.389 --> 00:02:51.430
I couldn't get the rubber gloves thing at all,

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:55.099
and I thought maybe they'd been doing the washing and just come out

00:02:55.099 --> 00:02:56.859
quickly or something and then

00:02:56.859 --> 00:02:59.080
someone said no, it was because you were shaking hands with

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:03.970
Gerry Adams. You should have been wearing rubber gloves
because he's such an evil person you oughtn't be shaking hands

00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:05.319
with him.

00:03:07.529 --> 00:03:11.579
So anyway, there's this

00:03:11.579 --> 00:03:16.539
whole business about meeting them and being able to talk to them

00:03:16.539 --> 00:03:21.139
allowed me over time to establish this relationship
where we started to have a real debate,

00:03:21.139 --> 00:03:25.029
and I was saying, and I understand why you may think

00:03:25.029 --> 00:03:26.949
that you may think that your violence brought

00:03:26.949 --> 00:03:29.379
this issue to people's attention,

00:03:29.379 --> 00:03:31.760
but believe me we are now at this stage

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:37.209
where your violence is the thing that stops this issue from being resolved.

00:03:37.209 --> 00:03:41.639
So it's interesting at both levels. It's difficult to answer your question.

00:03:41.639 --> 00:03:45.779
Yes, you have to bring it to people's attention. Maybe
violence isn't the only way you can do it,

00:03:45.779 --> 00:03:48.499
but the second thing is

00:03:48.499 --> 00:03:51.459
the act of engagement

00:03:51.459 --> 00:03:52.760
if it can establish

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:55.129
a relationship

00:03:55.129 --> 00:03:55.989
means

00:03:55.989 --> 00:03:58.189
that suddenly

00:03:58.189 --> 00:04:00.779
the power of persuasion is at least on the table.

00:04:00.779 --> 00:04:03.450
And I think in the end what Gerry Adams and Martin McGuinness needed

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:05.400
due to huge convincing by me,

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:07.190
I think they were

00:04:07.190 --> 00:04:09.659
coming to their own conclusion.

00:04:09.659 --> 00:04:12.359
Finally what clinched the Northern Ireland deal

00:04:12.359 --> 00:04:14.069
was the IRA just saying

00:04:14.069 --> 00:04:15.309
okay we're

00:04:15.309 --> 00:04:16.449
we're going away.

00:04:16.449 --> 00:04:17.609
You know, we're not surrendering,

00:04:17.609 --> 00:04:20.169
we're just disappearing.

00:04:20.169 --> 00:04:22.180
And actually that was

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:25.250
then the moment when unionism was faced

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:26.889
with its moment of truth

00:04:26.889 --> 00:04:30.059
because then the entire justification for

00:04:30.059 --> 00:04:31.539
the refusal

00:04:31.539 --> 00:04:34.129
was then moved, and that was the moment of
which

00:04:34.129 --> 00:04:38.900
Ian Paisley had to decide and be very decided the right way whether

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:41.069
really the problem was violence or

00:04:41.069 --> 00:04:43.349
really the problem was

00:04:43.349 --> 00:04:44.380
they weren't of the same tribe.

